To set priors on RW1 and. RW2 use f(…, scale.model=T). As this scale it so the the precision can be interpreted as a marginal precision. There is a tutorial on this issue at r-inla.org <http://r-inla.org>. otherwise, there is no control of what is going on.

As Finn said, there is a reason why we haven’t implemented P-splines and friends, but use RW1/RW2 and the SPDE-models.

H

